messages:
dmitry.customer: Hi team — hitting a 400 when calling tool via TS/Go SDKs if the tool arg contains certain emoji (works from python). Example payload attached.

alice.support: sorry to hear that, can you paste a minimal repro (request body + sdk version)? also which model/runtime?

dmitry.customer: payload (ts client):
```json
{
  "tool_name": "annotate",
  "args": {
    "text": "Flags: 🏳️‍⚧️ — appears to trigger validation"
  }
}
```
using @redwood/sdk-js 0.19.2 and redwood-go 0.8.1. Python client 0.19.2 works fine.

ben.eng: thanks. can you share the raw request/response from the failing client (the exact bytes sent and the API response body)? do you have the server error id?

dmitry.customer: here's the raw request body as logged from node (content-length redacted):
```
{"tool_name":"annotate","args":{"text":"Flags: 🏳️\u200d⚧️ — appears to trigger validation"}}
```
and response: 400 Bad Request {"error":"tool args failed schema validation","details":"invalid UTF-8 sequence at offset 23"}

clare.ml-sdk: hmmm interesting. note the \u200d (ZWJ) expansion in the node log — JS printed an escaped form. That suggests one of two things: either the SDK is pre-encoding strings into a byte blob (and something in the Go/TS encoder is mangling surrogate pairs), or downstream validation expects a normalized form.

alice.support: can you reproduce with a minimal TS script? if so we'll escalate to eng and create an incident.

dmitry.customer: yes minimal repro (node):
```js
const { Redwood } = require('@redwood/sdk');
const r = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW });
await r.callTool('annotate', { text: 'Flags: 🏳️‍⚧️' });
```
error -> 400 same as above. Go repro similar (fmt.Println) where string seems to be split into invalid runes before marshalling.

ben.eng: assigning to eng-infra. initial hypothesis: TS/Go SDKs have a path that converts strings -> []byte -> base64 for toolcall payloads, and the conversion uses incorrect rune handling on surrogate pairs/astral-plane emojis. Python path uses unicode-safe json and avoids the conversion, hence works.

clare.ml-sdk: short-term workaround: normalize or base64 the arg on the client side. example:
```js
const raw = 'Flags: 🏳️‍⚧️';
const b64 = Buffer.from(raw, 'utf8').toString('base64');
await r.callTool('annotate', { text_b64: b64 });
// server-side decode before passing to tool
```
this avoids hitting the broken codepath. please also try using String.prototype.normalize('NFC') to collapse sequences.

dmitry.customer: base64 workaround works for me, thanks. not ideal but unblocks.

ben.eng: thanks — creating ISSUE #INC-2026 and PR draft to fix rune handling in ts/go SDKs, will try to get a patch into a staging deploy today. cc @clare.ml-sdk.

deploy-bot: Staging deploy queued for sha@staging (PR #4253) — ETA ~15m :rocket:

ben.eng: update: patch landed on main that forces utf8-safe encoding and adds a unit test with 👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 and ZWJ sequences. publishing patch release 0.19.3 for ts and 0.8.2 for go.

dmitry.customer: verified 0.19.3 TS fix — no more 400s, thanks all :tada:

alice.support: marking resolved, follow-up: add an integration test that sends emoji+ZWJ sequences as part of our toolcall regression suite.
